From f7c2aec397acdc24752b4278c512bfd30023acbf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunrisepeak <speakshen@163.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 04:05:01 +0900
Subject: [clangd] One module that does not compile leaves the others

A prerequisite set was all or nothing: one module that failed to compile
left every importer with no module at all, not even std, so completion
answered nothing and every import was unresolved.

The set now holds the modules that did build. A module that failed, and any
module that imports it, are left out and reported, one line each, with the
compile's first error at info (an in-process build only said to look at a
verbose log). Importers are parsed with the rest; the import of a failed
module is diagnosed where it is. The set is not built again at every request
while the failed unit is unchanged, and is stale once its source changes, so
an edit that fixes it is picked up. A cancelled build still cancels the set.
